@startuml
title UC-06 - aws-eks happy path
autonumber
actor Developer
control DeploymentService as Service
control PlanningService as Planner
control ImplicitResourceEnricher as Enricher
control ResourceProvisioningService as Provisioner
boundary TerraformExecutor as Terraform
control OutputBindingResolver as Resolver
control WorkloadRenderer as Renderer
boundary WorkloadDeployer as K8s
database DeploymentRepository as Repo

Developer -> Service: DeployWorkload(Score, app, env)
Service -> Repo: Create PLANNING [MS-01]
Service -> Planner: Plan(request) [MS-02..MS-04]
Planner -> Enricher: Enrich(profile=aws-eks) [MS-05]
Enricher --> Planner: env/generation VPC + env/generation EKS + env/generation namespace
Planner -> Planner: Match Definitions; validate VPC/EKS Connection equals Environment binding [BR-20]
note right of Planner
Empty VPC/EKS keys inherit pinned READY Environment AWS account.
Malformed conflicting winner fails without fallback. All AWS nodes inherit same account/region.
end note
Planner --> Service: Humanitec-shaped Delta + graph:\nworkload -> namespace -> EKS -> VPC\nworkload -> Aurora -> VPC [MS-03..MS-08]
Service -> Renderer: Required score-k8s bundle/binary preflight
Service -> Repo: Admit Environment owner/fence under pinned versions
Service -> Provisioner: Provision(resource batches, owner/fence) [MS-09]
Provisioner -> Terraform: Provision(VPC, pinned Environment AWS account)
Terraform --> Provisioner: vpc outputs
Provisioner -> Terraform: Provision(EKS, vpc outputs, pinned Environment AWS account)
Terraform --> Provisioner: cluster target outputs
Provisioner -> Terraform: Provision(Aurora, vpc outputs, pinned Environment AWS account)
Terraform --> Provisioner: postgres outputs
Provisioner -> Terraform: Provision(namespace, completed EKS target)
Terraform --> Provisioner: namespace output
Provisioner -> Terraform: Redis: ElastiCache or in-cluster module by class
Terraform --> Provisioner: Redis outputs
Provisioner --> Service: outputs + EKS target
Service -> Resolver: ResolveWorkloadBindings(postgres + Redis outputs) [MS-10]
Resolver --> Service: Resolved target workload
Service -> Renderer: score-k8s Render(pinned bundle, output-only bindings, requests/limits) [MS-11]
Renderer --> Service: Service/Deployment manifests
Service -> K8s: Apply(EKS target, manifests)
Service -> K8s: WaitReady(target workload)
K8s --> Service: Ready
Service -> Repo: Commit set/resources/workloads/SUCCEEDED [MS-12]
Service --> Developer: DeploymentResult [MS-13]
note over Developer, Service
Acceptance verification repeats this operation for
backend, worker and frontend through existing forms.
Then browser submits job and verifies PostgreSQL + Redis use.
end note
@enduml
